ga4e(){return"Specify equipment info that your workers need to check, or issues that can be marked"},
ga7X(){return'Any information that cannot indicate an error by itself. For example: "username", "location", "firmware version"'},
ga7V(){return'A check that can be passed or failed. When completing checks, workers can provide problem details if any. In this case, the check will display as an issue. For example: "displayed on map", "connection works"'},
ga7Y(){return'An attribute indicating a problem in any case, even if no details are specified. Unlike the "check" type, this attribute must be removed from the equipment once the problem is resolved. For example: "physical damage"'},
ga98(){return"Settings & Help"},
gUg(){return"Help"},
ga7s(){return'"Tal" is a system for storing and tracking equipment information in your warehouse, designed to modern standards of convenience and safety, taking into account your requirements and feedback. Tal is developed every day (well, mostly nights). To contact me, write to animpafstd@gmail.com.'},
ga7O(){return"Frequently Asked Questions"},
ga7x(){return"What can I do in Tal?"},
ga7H(){return"First and foremost, Tal is a database. Here you can save information, check results, and found issues, as well as track the history of all these changes to detect data problems and locate equipment."},
ga7C(){return"We used to work in Excel and SAP. Why change anything?"},
ga7M(){return"The main goals of Tal are to improve the traceability of changes, provide a clear picture of issues in the warehouse, allow workers to easily find information, and update it quickly. Tal saves your time and nerves because it is developed specifically with your interests in mind, targeting and neutralizing the issues caused by current solutions."},
ga7z(){return"I find it inconvenient / I don't want to learn how to work here"},
ga7J(){return"This only means we have room for improvement! My job is not just to build a working system, but to make it convenient for everyone. Suggest your ideas - that way Tal will become exactly what you want it to be."},
ga7N(){return"Data"},
ga7A(){return"How do I find information about equipment?"},
ga7K(){return'In the application header, there is a search by groups, equipment types, serial numbers, and owners. You can also use the "Tables" button on the main screen.'},
ga7u(){return"How to update equipment info and what are attributes?"},
ga7E(){return'Practically all equipment information in Tal is organized in the form of attributes. You can think of attributes as columns in Excel, and for each item in the warehouse, these columns can be filled.\nOn the item page, you can add information (the add button under the "Attributes" header) or edit information marked by other users.\nAttributes can also be edited on the "Tables" page. Simply tap on the desired cell.'},
ga7t(){return'Why are there different types of attributes? What are "Info", "Check", and "Issue"?'},
ga7D(){return'For Tal to generate automatic reports about errors and missing information, it needs to understand exactly how to interpret the equipment info you add. It does this based on attribute types.\nYou should follow the on-screen prompts, and no additional help with this will be needed.\nIf you are an administrator and want to change the information workers need to check, go to the "Info to check" page on the main screen. There is more detailed help there on how Tal interprets attributes of different types.'},
ga7y(){return"Where is the change history?"},
ga7I(){return'The change history is stored on the "Journal" page. You can go there from the home page. Each change can be viewed in more detail by tapping on it. The page of each individual equipment item also has a history section.\nIf you are an administrator, your device stores its own copy of the database. In this case, for security reasons, other users\' changes are *NOT* automatically applied to your copy of the database.\nYou can tell you are an administrator by the orange (instead of blue) Tal logo in the top app bar on the main screen.'},
ga7B(){return"I need statistics / information about issues."},
ga7L(){return'The easiest way to find out about all issues in the warehouse is to go to the "Overview" page (the button on the main screen). On the "Info to check" page, you can find out statistics for each attribute (tap the button with scales next to the attribute you are interested in).'},
ga7P(){return"Security"},
ga7w(){return"How is the data I enter stored and transmitted?"},
ga7G(){return"Copies of the database and the change journal are stored in the Google Firebase system in encrypted form. The AES-256 standard is used for encryption.\nAlthough absolute security cannot be guaranteed, Tal takes many actions to minimize the risks of data loss and theft."},
ga7v(){return"How does Tal guarantee data safety?"},
ga7F(){return"Every day, changes made by workers are collected into a common file along with the active copy of the database. Encrypted backups of this file are saved in several locations.\nThus, the volume of data that could potentially be lost in case of an error is limited to the last working day."},
